GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC9 §3.2): sprite pieces of the lowest priority stay put.

The HP boxes are moved by rectangle (patch 0002); the player's platform reaches under its box,
and its tip (a 64x32 piece of priority 3) was moved with the box while the box was drawn. The
battle's boxes use priorities 0 and 1; priority 3 is the scenery under the battlers, never moved.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

--- a/src/GPU2D_Soft.h	2026-11-12 22:33:22.245055785 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU2D_Soft.h	2026-11-12 22:33:22.255652348 -0500
@@ -70,11 +70,13 @@
     // A sprite piece's x for this pass (moved when its centre lies in an ObjMove rectangle).
     // Shifted past the line's end, it lies outside this strip: -512 makes the callers skip it
     // (they skip x <= -width).
-    s32 SpriteX(u16 attrib1, u32 top, s32 width, s32 height) const
+    s32 SpriteX(u16 attrib1, u32 top, s32 width, s32 height, u16 attrib2) const
     {
         s32 x = (s32)(attrib1 << 23) >> 23;
         s32 dx = 0;
-        if (CurUnit->Num == 0)
+        // GoldLink: priority 3 is the scenery under the battlers (the player's platform reaches
+        // under its HP box): never moved with a box.
+        if (CurUnit->Num == 0 && ((attrib2 >> 10) & 3) != 3)
         {
             s32 cx = x + width / 2, cy = (s32)top + height / 2;
             for (int r = 0; r < ObjMoveCount; r++)
--- a/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp	2026-11-12 22:33:22.244994199 -0500
